          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef caruana_logloss_selector(P_oof, y_true, n_steps: int = 10) -> tuple[list[float], float, float]:\n    P = np.asarray(P_oof, dtype=float)\n    y = np.asarray(y_true, dtype=float)\n    M, n = P.shape\n    counts = np.zeros(M, dtype=int)\n    rsum = np.zeros(n, dtype=float)\n    def bce(p):\n        pc = np.clip(p, 1e-6, 1.0 - 1e-6)\n        return float(-np.mean(y * np.log(pc) + (1.0 - y) * np.log(1.0 - pc)))\n    for step in range(1, n_steps + 1):\n        losses = [bce((rsum + P[m]) / step) for m in range(M)]\n        bm = int(np.argmin(losses))\n        rsum += P[bm]\n        counts[bm] += 1\n    w = counts / float(n_steps)\n    p_ens = w @ P\n    pc_mat = np.clip(P, 1e-6, 1.0 - 1e-6)\n    logits = np.log(pc_mat / (1.0 - pc_mat))\n    p_logodds = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(w @ logits)))\n    return ([round(float(x), 2) for x in w], round(bce(p_ens), 4), round(bce(p_logodds), 4))\n```"
