          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef tail_sla_and_distill_loss(p_single_breach: float, k_models: int, z_teacher, z_student, y_hard, temp: float = 2.0, alpha: float = 0.7) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    p_par = 1.0 - (1.0 - float(p_single_breach)) ** int(k_models)\n    zt = np.asarray(z_teacher, dtype=float)\n    zs = np.asarray(z_student, dtype=float)\n    yh = np.asarray(y_hard, dtype=float)\n    sig = lambda x: 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-np.clip(x, -30.0, 30.0)))\n    p_s = np.clip(sig(zs), 1e-9, 1.0 - 1e-9)\n    hard_bce = float(-np.mean(yh * np.log(p_s) + (1.0 - yh) * np.log(1.0 - p_s)))\n    q_t = np.clip(sig(zt / temp), 1e-9, 1.0 - 1e-9)\n    p_t = np.clip(sig(zs / temp), 1e-9, 1.0 - 1e-9)\n    kl_t = float(np.mean(q_t * np.log(q_t / p_t) + (1.0 - q_t) * np.log((1.0 - q_t) / (1.0 - p_t))))\n    kd_loss = (1.0 - alpha) * hard_bce + alpha * (temp ** 2) * kl_t\n    return (round(p_par, 4), round(kd_loss, 4))\n```"
